Stop One's installers when an actual NAND erase operation fails.

Normal erase skips known bad blocks before mtd_erase(). A new -EIO from
that operation is an erase failure, not a successful skip. Propagate it so
the NOR, NAND and UART installers do not continue writing or report success.
In particular, their image readback cannot detect an unerased block beyond
the image length. Keep normal bad-block handling and other boards unchanged.
Preserve upstream -EIO handling for explicit manual erase.dontskipbad;
none of the product installers uses that mode.

--- a/cmd/mtd.c
+++ b/cmd/mtd.c
@@ -689,7 +689,7 @@
 		}
 
 		ret = mtd_erase(mtd, &erase_op);
-		if (ret && ret != -EIO)
+		if (ret && (ret != -EIO || !scrub))
 			break;
 
 		len -= mtd->erasesize;
@@ -700,7 +700,7 @@
 
 	led_activity_off();
 
-	if (ret && ret != -EIO)
+	if (ret && (ret != -EIO || !scrub))
 		ret = CMD_RET_FAILURE;
 	else
 		ret = CMD_RET_SUCCESS;
